title: Woven Basket
---
completion_date: 2025-11-28
---
craft_type: basketweaving
---
body:

Karen took basketweaving class and enjoyed it so much she wanted to continue it at home, so she talked me into giving it a try and splitting the cost of materials. (Not hard, since I'd been interested in trying it for a while)

The strips are made of rattan and soaked in water to make them pliable for weaving. The clips act as extra hands to hold everything in place while you wedge the next layer in place, often with the help of an awl.

My favourite clever bit was the split vertical spoke. We wanted an over-under pattern for the sides, which requires an odd number of spokes so that each layer goes over where the last one went under. However, we're guaranteed to have an even number of spokes since each reed going across the bottom produces two vertical spokes. Solution: split one of them to make an odd number.

Like pottery, I didn't like having my hands wet for long periods and don't have a lot of use for baskets. I enjoyed the process a lot more, probably because it was an excuse to spend time with a friend.
